### Follow the below instructions after installing off-the-shelf Sketch

### Building sketch-frontend with LTC

This project depends on the academic library `ltl2ba4j` available in (i.e., is not available in Maven Central): 
https://www.sable.mcgill.ca/~ebodde/rv/ltl2ba4j/  
We included the required JAR in this repository:

sketch-frontend/c-lib/ltl2ba4j.jar

Before building, you must install this JAR into the project-local Maven repository.

#### One-time setup

From the `c-lib` directory inside `sketch-frontend`, run:

>>> cd sketch-frontend/c-lib

>>> mvn install:install-file \
  -Dmaven.repo.local=../m2 \
  -Dfile=ltl2ba4j.jar \
  -DgroupId=org.rwth.i2 \
  -DartifactId=ltl2ba4j \
  -Dversion=1.0.0 \
  -Dpackaging=jar \
  -DgeneratePom=true


This installs ltl2ba4j into the project-local Maven repository (./m2), which is required because the Makefile overrides the default Maven repository location.

Build and run

After the setup step, you can build and run normally. For instance, to run the arbiter benchmark:

make run-local-seq EXEC_ARGS="benchmarks/ltlmonit/infinite/arbiter.sk"

No additional configuration should be necessary as long as c-lib/ltl2ba4j.jar is present and the m2 directory is kept with the project.
